    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d622">

                <pb facs="0496" n="488" sameAs="frus:frus1937v04/pg488"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.115 Panay/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commander of the United States Yangtze Patrol</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Marquart</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of Naval Operations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Leahy</hi>)<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d622-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Above
                                Nanking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-12-13T10:03:00+08:00">December 13 [?], 1937—10:03
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received December 12—10:06 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Message received by telephone from Nanking [:] <hi rendition="#italic">Panay</hi>
                    bombed and sunk at mileage 221 above Woosung, 54 survivors many badly wounded
                    now ashore at Hohsien, Anhwei. H. M. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Bee</hi> will
                    proceed this point to assist and bring survivors to Wuhu, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Oahu</hi> fueling Kiukiang preparatory departing Wuhu,
                    names of personnel lost not known. Atcheson safe, Captain<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d622-f2"/> has broken leg, further information will be forwarded
                    when received.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d622-f1" n="52" type="source" xml:id="d622-f1-content">
